**Note on the fix at `eeb556e`: a trust trade-off worth recording.**

The fix is correct for the reported grief: an outsider can no longer cancel a soft-cap-met Standard/BondTreasury launch. A side effect: if finalization of such a launch ever fails **permanently**, contributors' ETH can only be released by `protocolAuthority` calling `cancelUnfinalizedLaunch`. Before the fix this was self-service after `endTime + 7 days`.

**Suggestion (optional):** add a long permissionless backstop so contributor refunds never depend solely on the authority, e.g.

```solidity
if (buildRouter == address(0) && refundableETH >= launch.softCap && msg.sender != protocolAuthority) {
    if (block.timestamp < uint256(launch.endTime) + 30 days) revert Unauthorized();
}
```

The 30-day window is long enough that a temporary finalization block cannot be used for griefing.
